      "text": "To determine the cost of the gas used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total distance traveled.\n2. Determine the amount of gas used.\n3. Calculate the cost of the gas used.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total distance traveled.**\n\nThe initial odometer reading is 74,568 miles, and the final odometer reading is 74,592 miles. The distance traveled is:\n\\[\n74,592 - 74,568 = 24 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the amount of gas used.**\n\nRyosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon. Therefore, the amount of gas used is:\n\\[\n\\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{28 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = \\frac{24}{28} \\text{ gallons} = \\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the cost of the gas used.**\n\nThe price of one gallon of gas is $4.05. Therefore, the cost of the gas used is:\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{7} \\text{ gallons} \\times 4.05 \\text{ dollars per gallon} = \\frac{6 \\times 4.05}{7} \\text{ dollars} = \\frac{24.30}{7} \\text{ dollars} \\approx 3.4714285714285715 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest cent, the cost is:\n\\[\n3.47 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nThus, the cost of the gas that was used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work is \\(\\boxed{3.47}\\).",
